{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:stage1-codex-02\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:2e26bf5ece15be03717f\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The stated task requires an occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\",\"observed_value\":\"entire scheduled survey network\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"task.md\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":1,\"quoted_text\":\"Using the supplied coastal-station base workflow, produce a revised selected occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report defines the target as all 96 scheduled stations and selects a rate whose denominator is those same 96 stations, not the 72 retained stations.\",\"observed_value\":\"18/96 = 0.1875\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":4,\"end_line\":4,\"quoted_text\":\"Target population: all 96 scheduled coastal stations in the survey network.\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":14,\"end_line\":15,\"quoted_text\":\"Exposure denominator: all 96 scheduled stations, so the 24 omitted stations stay in the denominator and contribute zero observed occurrences.\\n[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: 18 occurrences divided by 96 scheduled stations = 0.1875 (18.75 occurrences per 100 scheduled stations).\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"A retained subset exists and all observed occurrences come from it, creating a concrete possibility of the scoped error if the selected denominator had been 72.\",\"observed_value\":{\"retained\":72,\"omitted\":24,\"observed_occurrences\":18},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":9,\"end_line\":11,\"quoted_text\":\"Stations passing the signal screen: 72\\nStations omitted by the signal screen and left without a usable observation: 24\\nOccurrences observed among the retained stations: 18\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to falsify the bounded verified-good judgment by checking whether the selected result divided the 18 retained-station occurrences by the 72 stations passing the screen. The selected-rate lines instead explicitly retain all 96 scheduled stations in the denominator and report 18/96, so the retained-subset-denominator mismatch is not demonstrated.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"},{\"case_id\":\"case:b036fd64c647dfd93e35\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The scientific question is explicitly conditional on passing the prespecified signal screen, so the complete scheduled network is not the requested denominator.\",\"observed_value\":\"conditional on passing the screen\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"task.md\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":1,\"quoted_text\":\"Build a coastal-station workflow whose scientific question is the occurrence rate conditional on passing a prespecified signal screen.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report consistently defines the target as the 72 signal-eligible stations and reports the selected result only among that eligible population.\",\"observed_value\":\"18/72 = 25%\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":4,\"end_line\":4,\"quoted_text\":\"Target population: 72 signal-eligible stations that passed the prespecified signal screen.\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":8,\"end_line\":8,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was 18/72 = 25%.\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The workflow also identifies a larger scheduled network and 24 stations outside the eligible set, which would be relevant if the selected claim purported to cover the complete domain.\",\"observed_value\":{\"scheduled\":96,\"outside_eligible\":24},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":3,\"end_line\":5,\"quoted_text\":\"Scheduled network: 96 stations.\\nTarget population: 72 signal-eligible stations that passed the prespecified signal screen.\\nPlanned-unit accounting: 18 eligible stations with an occurrence, 54 eligible stations without an occurrence, and 24 scheduled stations outside the eligible set and not assessed for occurrence.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to falsify the bounded verified-good judgment by looking for a selected claim generalized to all 96 scheduled stations despite using 72 as its denominator. Although the report discloses the 96-station network, both its target and selected-result wording remain expressly conditional on the 72 signal-eligible stations, so the scoped mismatch is not demonstrated.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"},{\"case_id\":\"case:35069763f06891dba5a3\",\"verdict\":\"demonstrated_issue\",\"bounded_statement\":\"The selected result claims an occurrence rate for the entire 96-station scheduled survey network but divides the 18 observed occurrences only by the 72 stations retained after screening, excluding 24 scheduled stations from the exposure denominator.\",\"root_cause\":\"The workflow sets the selected denominator to SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS and interpolates that retained-subset count into a result labeled as applying to the entire scheduled survey network.\",\"issue_class\":\"issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain\",\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The stated task requires one occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\",\"observed_value\":\"entire scheduled survey network\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"task.md\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":1,\"quoted_text\":\"Build a compact coastal-station workflow that reports one occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report defines the target population as all 96 scheduled stations while accounting for only 72 retained stations and 24 omitted stations.\",\"observed_value\":{\"target\":96,\"retained\":72,\"omitted\":24},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":4,\"end_line\":4,\"quoted_text\":\"Target population: all 96 scheduled coastal stations in the survey network.\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":8,\"end_line\":10,\"quoted_text\":\"Scheduled stations (planned units): 96\\nStations passing the signal screen: 72\\nStations omitted by the signal screen: 24\"}]},{\"description\":\"The selected result explicitly labels its claim as covering the entire scheduled network but uses the 72 retained stations as its denominator.\",\"observed_value\":\"18/72 = 0.25\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":14,\"end_line\":15,\"quoted_text\":\"Exposure denominator: the 72 stations retained after the signal screen.\\n[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: 18 occurrences divided by 72 retained stations = 0.25 (25.00 occurrences per 100 stations).\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow directly constructs the complete-network claim using SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS as the divisor.\",\"observed_value\":\"SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":22,\"end_line\":23,\"quoted_text\":\"DENOMINATOR_LINE = f'Exposure denominator: the {SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS} stations retained after the signal screen.' + LF\\nSELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS} retained stations = {SELECTED_RATE_FRACTION} ({SELECTED_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 stations).' + LF\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The omitted stations have unassessed occurrence values, which could support a separately stated retained-subset estimand; however, the visible task and selected claim do not state that conditional estimand.\",\"observed_value\":\"occurrence_flag=NA for omitted station\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/data.csv\",\"start_line\":5,\"end_line\":5,\"quoted_text\":\"CS-004,North,yes,omitted,screen_fail_low_snr,NA\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":10,\"end_line\":11,\"quoted_text\":\"Stations omitted by the signal screen: 24\\nOccurrences observed among the retained stations: 18\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to falsify the issue by checking whether the 18/72 result was explicitly conditional on passing the screen or whether an approved target change justified excluding the 24 omitted stations. Instead, the report calls the target all 96 stations, calls 18/72 the rate for the entire network, and states that no approved method deviation exists.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}"}}
